==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[level]] [[playing field]]}}

# A [[situation]] which offers no [[advantage]] to any particular [[person]] or [[side]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=OECD|title=Competitive Neutrality{{...|: Maintaining a Level Playing Field between Public and Private Business}}|publisher=OECD Publishing|isbn=9789264178953|page=9|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=DFI4qtJwTasC&pg=PA9&dq=%22level+playing+field%22&hl=&cd=18&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22level%20playing%20field%22&f=false|text=Although the political commitment to maintaining a '''level playing field''' is generally strong, government commercial activities may damage the competition landscape either due to deliberate or unintentional departures from neutral practices.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2024 March 20|title=Network News: Freight still needs a '''level playing field''', MPs hear from Rail Partners|journal=RAIL|issue=1005|page=11|text=Although the government has significantly reduced its UK growth targets to 75% by 2050 from the heady heights of trebling it in ten years at the beginning of privatisation, the rail freight industry is calling on all politicians to create a '''level playing field''' with road haulage.}}

